      "part": "worked_solution",
      "original_record": "history",
      "value": "Consider the line $y=3x+1.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge 3x+1.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=2.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 3x+1 \\\\ y\\ge 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "original_html_sha256": "e035ac78ad8e986a4fc0c76ba6bd5e4612fc821efae83b7b2613f6a3c68ae8e2",
